<title>CHILE: Chile Jan-April bank profits climb 35 pct.</title>
<headline>Chile Jan-April bank profits climb 35 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's banking and financial sector reported net earnings in the four months to April of 99.4 billion pesos, up 35 percent from the same period last year, said the Banking and Financial Institutions Superintendency.</p>
<p>Loan portfolios swelled 11.4 percent with trade loans up 12.3 percent while consumer loans climbed 30 percent from the same period of 1996.</p>
<p>The following are the net earnings of individual banks in the four months to April.</p>
<p>			 April 1997	    April 1996</p>
<p>Bhif			4.24		    n/a</p>
<p>de A. Edwards	   6.93		    6.3</p>
<p>de Chile		 21.88		    7.4</p>
<p>de Credito e Inv	8.07		    7.1</p>
<p>Santiago		 20.59		    n/a</p>
<p>Santander-Chile	 8.72		    n/a</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures are in billions of pesos. The 1996 figures are in peso terms from that year and are not expressed in 1997 pesos.</p>
<p>Banco de Chile 1996 figure takes into account subordinated debt repayment.</p>
</text>
